# Component fscboot-a of peer a (DigiGilde voorbeeld) in deployment ${DEPLOYMENT_A} of project ${PROJECT}:
# the bootstrap of the peer (bootstrap.sh), next to its manager and
# controller, whose internal APIs on port 8444 nothing outside the deployment
# reaches. It registers and publishes the service of this instance, asks for
# a connection to the service of every other peer, and prints the rows for
# grip's peer registry in its log.
# Image: ghcr.io/<repository>/fsc-bootstrap. No port and not published.
# Services: attachments, for the files below, and health-check with scheme
# none, as nothing listens. Attachments: internal-* of upload/<deployment>/fscboot-a at
# /etc/fsc/a/internal/* (the internal CA and the admin client certificate).
# Fill in with `just zad-fsc-env <deployment>`, which substitutes these
# placeholders and no others:
#   envsubst '${BASE_DOMAIN} ${PROJECT} ${DEPLOYMENT_DIR} ${DEPLOYMENT_A} ${DEPLOYMENT_B} ${DEPLOYMENT_D}'
# The values belong to the component itself, not to its layer in deployment
# ${DEPLOYMENT_A}: the component runs only there, and its first deploy must
# find them. zadctl env add -c fscboot-a --env-file <file>, without --deployment.

PEER=a
# The peers of the group; a b d once Ministerie van BZK voorbeeld joins.
PEERS=a d
BASE_DOMAIN=${BASE_DOMAIN}
PROJECT=${PROJECT}
DEPLOYMENT_A=${DEPLOYMENT_A}
DEPLOYMENT_B=${DEPLOYMENT_B}
DEPLOYMENT_D=${DEPLOYMENT_D}
TLS_ROOT_CERT=/etc/fsc/a/internal/ca.pem
TLS_CERT=/etc/fsc/a/internal/cert.pem
TLS_KEY=/etc/fsc/a/internal/key.pem
